@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

title One migration step end to end, and the checks that prove it landed

start

:Move the files.\nRoutes leave Code/ConversationalUX/FindCareChat/backend/app.py\nand land in the FindCare/ feature directory that owns them;

:Update deployment_architecture.json.\nEvery moved file's source_location is rewritten.\nIts content_hash follows the file;

partition "build_chathealthy.py" {
  :Validate the manifest against its schema\n(RecordLoader.validate_architecture);
  :Materialise the source tree.\nlocal reads the working tree,\ndev/qa/prod read origin/<branch>;
  :Refresh content_hash for every referenced file\nfrom disk, CRLF-normalised;
  note right
    This rewrite runs BEFORE the gate below, so on
    dev/qa/prod a hash that drifted is snapshotted
    rather than refused. Only --env local still
    fails on drift, because there the refresh and
    the gate read two different trees.
  end note

  if (Crosswalk gate) then (a declared\nsource_location\nis not on disk)
    :REJECT — "source_location ... not present on disk";
    stop
  else (every declaration\nresolves)
  endif

  if (preflight_undefined_names) then (unresolved name\nin a scan root)
    :exit 3;
    stop
  else (clean)
  endif

  :Stage each package from the declared file list,\nrun vite, write build.json\n(env, git sha, build_number);
}

partition "deploy_chathealthy.py" {
  if (staleness gate\nagainst build.json) then (wrong env, sha behind\nHEAD, or build_number\nolder than the counter)
    :ERROR — rebuild;
    stop
  else (current)
  endif
  :Install each package to the target that declares it;
  :Poll the target's /health until it reports\nthe build_number just deployed;
  note right
    The target says which build it carries.
    The deploy reads that back rather than
    assuming the install took.
  end note
}

:Conformance gate reports the new number.\nOne more of the twelve cells is a real tool,\nand app.py is shorter by the routes that moved;

stop

floating note left
  Nothing in the build refuses a file that
  exists on disk and is declared nowhere -- an
  undeclared file is silently not shipped. That
  is BUG-011, and it is why a migration step
  needs the conformance gate rather than the
  build alone to say the move is complete.
end note

@enduml
